{
  "rationale": "The plant is split into sensing and motion capability so the supervisor can react to uncontrollable obstacle observations before issuing one-shot motion pulses. The specifications encode a conservative-but-progressive exploration policy: random_walk in clear/search mode, short move_forward after a clear pulse, directed turn recovery on obstacle_left/right/front, and full_rotate only as a last-resort blocked recovery. Action states use self-loops on non-critical path_clear to preserve intended one-shot commands under the stated runtime semantics.",
  "strategy": [
    "Model perception as uncontrollable environment updates and motion as controllable one-shot actions.",
    "Use small deterministic specifications to bind clear sensing to exploration actions and obstacle sensing to directed recovery turns, with a sparse last-resort full_rotate path."
  ],
